    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85532" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ̆-χαλκος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abounding in copper</i> or
				<i>bronze,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύχρυσος π.,</span> of Troy, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.289
			</span></i>; of Sidon, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.425
			</span></i>; of Dolon, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.315
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>wrought of bronze, brazen,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.504
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					1.18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
